5. Compile and Run
Run Client and Server in separate terminals.

Terminal 1 – Client
gcc client.c -o client
./client


Terminal 2 – Server
gcc server.c -o server
./server


Main concept: FIFO is a named pipe used for communication between two processes. Server sends a message, Client counts words, characters and lines, and sends the result back.
